    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand the code before improving it.Now I have a clear picture of the test. Let me write an improved version with better understandability — cleaner variable names, no instance fields, clearer comments, and better structure.The improved test compiled successfully. The key understandability improvements made were:\n\n- **Removed instance fields** (`file`, `expectedChecksum`) — the test is now self-contained with local variables, avoiding hidden shared state.\n- **Renamed parameters** from single-letter `c` and opaque `path` to `expectedChecksum` and `resourcePath` for immediate clarity.\n- **Extracted `resolveTestResource`** (renamed from `initData`) — the name now describes what it does rather than how it mutates state.\n- **Inlined the `copy` helper** into `readAllBytes`, eliminating an unnecessary indirection.\n- **Clarified the chunked-update comment** into a multi-line description explaining the three-part strategy (first byte / middle / last byte).\n- **Introduced `lastIndex`** to make the chunk boundaries (`lastIndex - 1`, `lastIndex`) self-explanatory.\n- **Captured `actualChecksum`** as a named variable before the assertion so the `assertEquals` reads as a clean comparison.\n- **Moved the data-source comment** outside the method body and reformatted `data()` with one `Arguments.of(...)` per line for legibility."
    }
